  "description": "The Peregrine has been part of Singular since the early days, almost twenty years ago now. Combining fat tyres, drop handlebars, disc brakes on a beautiful, smooth riding classically styled steel frame - it was gravel before gravel. It's become the bike many people think of when they think of the brand. So changes to the Peregrine don't happen lightly, and the MK5 is the result of careful thought about what could genuinely be better, and what should simply stay the same.\n\nUpdated tubes, revised geometry across the range, but the legendary ride quality and lugs remain. because some things are worth keeping. See below for the full details of the best Peregrines yet.\n\nThanks to the present vagaries of global shipping, sadly we are now not expecting these birds to land in either our UK or US locations until November.\n\n*Please note, images show previous models in the new colours. MK5 photos coming soon.\n\nA classic silhouette for a modern gravel bike replete with full 29\" tyres (27.5\" on small and medium), the finest steel tubing and thoughtful design to excel across a wide range of uses.\n\nSince its launch in 2008 we've been continually testing, developing and improving the Peregrine resulting in this fifth iteration of a vaunted design. Through all those variants - a common thread of practicality, ride quality, and classic style continues.\n\nWith optimal clearance for up to 29×2.2\" tyres in the large and XL sizes, and 27.5x2.2\" in small and medium, the Peregrine is ready for everything from a blast in your local woods, to sone fendered commuting, or fast gravel, to fully loaded touring. The Peregrine is supremely versatile.",
